  "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented payment terms support. Here's what was added:\n\n**Updated `src/dates.js`**\n- Added `lastDayOfMonth(date)` function to calculate the last day of a month\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`**\n- Modified `createInvoice()` to accept optional `terms` parameter ('NET14', 'NET30', or 'EOM')\n- Defaults to 'NET30' if no terms specified\n- Calculates `dueDate` based on terms:\n  - **NET14**: 14 days after issue date\n  - **NET30**: 30 days after issue date\n  - **EOM**: Last day of the issue date's month\n- Returns `TERMS_INVALID` for unknown terms\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`**\n- Added `TERMS_INVALID` error code\n\n**Added comprehensive tests:**\n- 13 new tests in `test/invoices.test.js` covering:\n  - Default NET30 behavior\n  - All three term types (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n  - Invalid terms rejection\n  - Month/year boundary handling\n  - Leap year considerations\n  - All invoice properties preservation\n\n- 7 new tests in `test/dates.test.js` covering:\n  - Last day calculation for all month types\n  - Different starting days of month\n  - Year boundaries\n  - Leap and non-leap year Februaries\n\nAll 181 tests pass. The implementation is ready to commit.",
